    "heading": "Segregation of duties: the Kevin Park conflict",
    "body": "Kestrel's segregation-of-duties (SoD) rule: on the Identity Directory (A-007), no one may hold two or more of provision accounts, approve access and administer audit logs. Someone who can approve and provision can give anyone access with no second pair of eyes. Someone who also administers the audit logs can hide it.\n\nKevin Park (E-009) holds all three, the only conflict in the data. The surrounding evidence:\n- He granted himself approve access (2025-11-03) and administer audit logs (2026-02-17).\n- He granted 107 of the 171 permissions in the file, 62.6%.\n- He reviewed his own access in the Q3 review (AR-001).\n- He is the manager of record for vendor engineer E-015, and the reviewer of that account (AR-002, overdue).\n\nNone of this says Kevin did anything wrong. It says nobody could tell if he had, which is issue I-01. The fix: remove approve access and administer audit logs from E-009; give approval to the business owners and audit-log administration to security, Sam Okafor (E-020); re-approve his remaining rights through Daniel Osei (E-004); and redo AR-001 with an independent reviewer."
